==English==
===Phrase=== {{infl|en|phrase|head=[[how]] [[do]] [[you]] [[like]] [[them]] [[apple]]s}}?

#{{idiom}} directed [[jestingly]] or [[mockingly]] at someone who has received [[surprising]] information, [[ridicule|ridiculing]] the situation
#:''"Our governor has just vetoed a bill that would offer more money to our schools. '''How do you like them apples'''?"''
#{{idiom}}''(Irish and Irish-American)'' Used after an actual or proposed action with which the listener might be displeased. Also used after refuting an argument.
#:''"I can't give you a raise now; if I did, this whole company would go bankrupt, and you wouldn't have a job at all. Now how do you like them apples?"''

